<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Frederick, Duke of Saxe-Altenburg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1763">1763</a>–<a href="/years/1834">1834</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Frederick, Duke of Saxe-Hildburghausen</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Frederick was Duke of Saxe-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hildburghausen">Hildburghausen</a> from 1780 and, after the Ernestine lands were rearranged in 1826, the first Duke of the new Saxe-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/altenburg">Altenburg</a>. His daughter Therese married Crown Prince Ludwig of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a> in 1810, and the horse race held to celebrate the wedding in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/munich">Munich</a> became the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oktoberfest">Oktoberfest</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/frederick-duke-of-saxe-altenburg.jpg" alt="Frederick, Duke of Saxe-Altenburg" width="320" height="385" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Carl Vogel (?) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:FriedrichHibuAltenburg.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
